[CHANGE] benchmarks/runs/semver_solver_deepseek_flash_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_pretense.py: Widen the modeled range-text domain required by the [from:pretense_coverage] scenarios on the impl unit: VALID_RANGE_TEXTS gains ^0.2.3, ^0.0.3, ^0.0.0 (caret widening on zero-major full versions), <1.x, <1.2.x (strict less-than wildcard expansion) and ~*, ~x (tilde on a bare wildcard major boundary); SAMPLE_RANGES gains the matching VersionRange records so range matching can be asserted on them; SAMPLE_VERSIONS gains 0.0.3, 0.2.3 and 0.3.0 so caret boundary witnesses are expressible as modeled version inputs.
[CHANGE] benchmarks/runs/semver_solver_deepseek_flash_1/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: Resolve all seven [from:pretense_coverage] deficits with added scenario executions in TestSemverSolverImplReal (no adapter require() guards). parse_range.malformed_syntax: violating(InvalidRangeError) scenarios for a multi-component numeric target (>=1.2.3.4) and a non-numeric target (>=v1.2.3). parse_range.comparators_and_prefixes: test_parse_range_caret_zero_major_full_versions parses ^0.2.3/^0.0.3/^0.0.0 and asserts the zero-major widening boundaries via satisfies (0.2.3 in, 0.3.0 out; 0.0.3 in, 0.1.0 out; 0.0.0 in, 0.0.3 out); test_parse_range_tilde_bare_wildcard parses ~* and ~x and asserts the bare-wildcard major boundary admits 0.0.0; test_parse_range_less_than_wildcard parses <1.x/<1.2.x and asserts 0.2.0 in / 1.0.0 out and 1.1.0 in / 1.2.3 out. solver.compatible_assignment: test_resolve_assigned_dependency_conflict now publishes alpha@2.0.0 plus beta@0.1.0 and beta@2.0.0 so alpha (one candidate) is assigned before beta and beta@2.0.0's alpha>=3.0.0 requirement conflicts with the already-assigned alpha before rolling back to beta@0.1.0. solver.unsatisfiable_conflict: new test_resolve_exhausts_candidates_before_conflict publishes alpha@1.0.0 and only the conflicting beta@2.0.0 so every candidate is rolled back and the search returns false before violating(ResolutionConflictError) is self-asserted. parse_version.leading_zero_grammar: test_parse_version_error_diagnostic_rendering instantiates the raised error record, asserts its structured message/raw_text attributes and renders its canonical diagnostic text. Companion model companions widened to model the new range texts and versions.
